## 1. Introduction

This report explores two possible career pathways in Darwin, Northern Territory: Report Writer and Business Analyst. The purpose of the research is to understand the duties, skills, software tools and qualifications commonly required for these roles.

The selected career roles are:

* **Primary Role:** Report Writer
* **Secondary Role:** Business Analyst

Job advertisements and career information available through employment platforms such as SEEK and LinkedIn were examined. The research was then used to create a three-week learning plan focused on developing practical skills relevant to both positions.

## 2. Career Research

### Primary Role – Report Writer

#### Role Overview

A Report Writer is responsible for turning research, business information and data into clear and professional documents. These reports may be prepared for managers, clients, government departments, project teams or other stakeholders.

The role requires strong writing ability, attention to detail and an understanding of how to organise complex information. A Report Writer may also review data, communicate with team members and edit documents before final submission.

#### Main Responsibilities

| Responsibility                | Description                                                             |
| ----------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Prepare professional reports  | Create business, project, research and technical reports                |
| Research information          | Collect relevant information from documents, databases and stakeholders |
| Review data                   | Examine data and identify important findings                            |
| Structure documents           | Organise information using headings, tables, charts and summaries       |
| Edit and proofread            | Correct grammar, spelling, formatting and inconsistencies               |
| Communicate with stakeholders | Confirm information and understand reporting requirements               |
| Manage deadlines              | Complete reports within agreed project timeframes                       |
| Present findings              | Explain important results and recommendations clearly                   |

A Report Writer must ensure that the final document is accurate, easy to understand and suitable for its intended audience.

### Secondary Role – Business Analyst

#### Role Overview

A Business Analyst studies an organisation’s processes, systems and business needs. The analyst communicates with stakeholders to identify problems and recommends solutions that can improve business performance.

The role often connects business staff with technical teams. Business Analysts document requirements, create workflow diagrams and support the implementation of new systems or processes.

#### Main Responsibilities

| Responsibility                 | Description                                                  |
| ------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------ |
| Identify business needs        | Understand the problems and goals of the organisation        |
| Gather requirements            | Interview stakeholders and document their expectations       |
| Analyse processes              | Review current workflows and identify inefficiencies         |
| Prepare documentation          | Create business requirements and functional documents        |
| Develop process diagrams       | Visually represent existing and proposed workflows           |
| Communicate with project teams | Work with managers, developers, testers and users            |
| Assist with testing            | Check whether a solution meets the documented requirements   |
| Recommend improvements         | Suggest changes to systems, processes or business operations |

Business Analyst positions commonly require strong communication, documentation, problem-solving and stakeholder-management skills.

## 3. Comparison of the Two Roles

| Report Writer                                            | Business Analyst                                                 |
| -------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Concentrates on preparing clear and professional reports | Concentrates on understanding and solving business problems      |
| Organises research, information and data                 | Analyses systems, processes and business requirements            |
| Produces reports, summaries and formal documents         | Produces requirements documents, user stories and process models |
| Requires advanced writing and editing skills             | Requires analytical and stakeholder-engagement skills            |
| Commonly uses Word, Excel and PowerPoint                 | Commonly uses Jira, Confluence, Visio, Excel and SQL             |
| Communicates findings through written reports            | Communicates proposed solutions to business and technical teams  |
| Checks document accuracy and consistency                 | Checks whether solutions satisfy business requirements           |

Although the roles have different areas of focus, both require clear communication, research, documentation, critical thinking and time-management skills.

