## 9. Conclusion

The career research shows that Report Writing and Business Analysis are closely connected through communication, research and professional documentation.

The Report Writer role is most suitable for developing strong writing, editing, formatting and information-presentation skills. The Business Analyst role adds analytical skills such as gathering requirements, examining business processes and recommending improvements.

During the next three weeks, the main focus will be developing professional report-writing skills, improving Microsoft Office knowledge and gaining introductory experience with GitHub, Jira, Visio, Confluence and SQL. The completed activities will also provide examples of work that can be included in a future professional portfolio.
